# FinanceAI ClickHouse Migration — Project Context

## Tech Stack
- Django 5.x, PostgreSQL 16, Celery + Redis, React frontend
- clickhouse-connect==0.15.1 already in requirements
- Existing partial ClickHouse scaffolding: apps/core/routers.py, apps/core/management/commands/init_clickhouse.py
- Docker Compose already exists

## Key Existing Files (DO NOT break these)
- apps/core/models.py:134 — AuditLog model (being replaced)
- apps/core/views/auth_views.py:167 — AuditLogListView (being rewritten)
- apps/invoices/views/analytics_views.py — all analytics views (being rewritten)
- apps/invoices/services.py — transition_expense() and other business logic
- js/Secondary.jsx:1126 — AuditScreen frontend
- docker-compose.yml — add ClickHouse service here

## Existing AI Pipeline Functions (wrap these, don't replace)
- apps/invoices/ai/ocr_pipeline.py
- apps/invoices/ai/anomaly_pipeline.py
- apps/invoices/ai/forecast_pipeline.py
- apps/invoices/ai/query_agent.py
- apps/invoices/ai/build_query_ai_suggestion()

## Coding Standards
- Use black formatting (88 char line length)
- Django imports: stdlib → third-party → django → local
- All models need Meta: db_table, ordering, verbose_name
- All views need explicit permission_classes
- All Celery tasks need explicit name= parameter
- Never use bare except:
- Type hints on all new functions
